---
title: "calculate_debt_value (Scallop Lend: Borrowing)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: total_debt = 0
    q_init --> q_iter: for each (coin_type, debt_amount) in obligation.debts
    q_iter --> q_get_price: get oracle_price(coin_type)
    q_get_price --> q_get_weight: get borrow_weight(coin_type)
    q_get_weight --> q_calc: weighted_debt = debt_amount * oracle_price * borrow_weight
    q_calc --> q_accum: total_debt = total_debt + weighted_debt
    q_accum --> q_iter: more debt types
    q_accum --> [*]: no more types, return total_debt

    note right of q_get_weight
        INV-001: borrow_weight >= 1 for all asset pools
        INV-002: volatile assets have higher borrow_weight (e.g. SUI=1.25 vs USDC=1.0)
        INV-003: debt_value = SUM(debt_i * price_i * borrow_weight_i) for all i
    end note

    note right of q_calc
        INV-004: Higher borrow_weight reduces effective borrowing capacity for volatile assets
        INV-005: debt_amount includes accrued interest
    end note
